    "published_source_revision": "6a888f9dc4155b9ec1407b27223eb37218957159",
    "source_path": "TranscendentalNakamaye/blueprint/src/hironaka-smooth-centre-real-domain-original-stalk-freeness-extension.tex",
    "source_sha256": "de5b6a5631c172d700cb459aee53c2537b04a9c46e34a9b1f1e06f3a43a1f4f3",
    "source_kind": "complete_original_statement_and_proof_fragment",
    "selected_original_source_sha256": "d8f29b05d632cdf957f056505ebfae42f54e3a8960d32bb30c310a5feb005fb2",
    "selected_original_source": "\\begin{lemma}[Every actual target point has the whole original fixed-flattening stalk dictionary]\n\\label{hir:real-domain-fixed-flattening-all-original-whole-stalks}\n\\source{bierstone-milman08-functoriality}\n\\uses{hir:real-centre-domain-original-pullback-coherence,hir:real-centre-domain-whole-nearby-translated-ideals,hir:nonlinear-nearby-actual-generator-transport,hir:nonlinear-nearby-original-whole-stalk-dictionary}\n\\lean{TranscendentalNakamaye.Pending.HironakaSmoothCentreRealDomainOriginalStalkFreeness.whole_original_stalk_dictionary_at_actual_target}\n\\leanok\nLet the original ideal be coherent and fix ANY genuine flattening whose\nsource lies in the real original chart target. At EVERY actual point of\nthis fixed flattening target, the entire actual translated flattened ideal\nmaps under the genuine recentered nonlinear germ equivalence to the WHOLE\noriginal fixed-chart stalk ideal at the actual inverse image point. Its\nwhole inverse ideal image is the corresponding entire comap. No different\nflattening, nearby ideal-map witness or global model coherence is assumed.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\nAt the actual inverse image point choose the original coherent ideal's true\nfinite holomorphic generators and complete local membership span. The real\ninverse chart is holomorphic at every point of the actual flattening target.\nIts actual pullback generators therefore present the existing flattened\nideal on a genuine smaller open containing the stated target point and\nmapping into the original generator domain. Translate these ACTUAL functions\nat that point to zero. The real finite-generator translation dictionary\nidentifies their entire ideal span with the WHOLE translated flattened\norigin ideal. The true original finite-generator dictionary in the fixed\nchart identifies its WHOLE original stalk with the entire chart-germ span\nof the same original functions. The actual recentered nonlinear germ\nequivalence maps each translated composite function germ to its true\noriginal chart-function germ. Mapping every finite ideal sum in both\ndirections therefore gives the whole ideal image equality. The nonlinear\ngerm map is a genuine ring equivalence, so applying its comap gives the\nentire inverse ideal equality. This argument is local at each actual point\nof one fixed target and asserts nothing outside that real domain.\n\\end{proof}\n",
    "destination_path": "blueprint/hironaka-original-fixed-flattening-stalk-dictionary-support.tex",
    "destination_sha256": "28c657e486750876328e845cdea57a82a182fe57b1d9f39aaebd19e4419300d2",
    "nodes": 1,
